# Angelina Hybrid Cloud — LOCAL instance cron fragment (Task 9.1)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# REVIEWABLE ARTIFACT — NOT installed automatically. See install-local-cron.sh
# and the apply plan in deploy/hybrid/APPLY_PLAN.md before applying to the VM.
#
# Times are in the VM's local timezone (Asia/Taipei, UTC+8), matching the
# existing 23:00 Daily_Push convention.
#
# This fragment adds ONE new job: the 06:00 bi-directional sync. It is additive
# and does not touch the existing 23:00 Daily_Push job or any other cron entry.
#
# Requirements: 5.1 (once-per-day sync at a configured off-peak time), 2.4
# (non-regression: existing local behavior untouched).
#
# NOTE ON THE 23:00 PUSH (for reviewer context, DO NOT duplicate):
#   The existing local crontab already runs the 23:00 Daily_Push. Task 9.1
#   item 1 (stamp heartbeat after a successful push) is handled *inside the
#   application* (app/daily_analysis.py now calls write_heartbeat() after a
#   successful Telegram send), so NO cron change is needed for the heartbeat.
#   The existing 23:00 line is intentionally NOT modified here.
#
#   If you later want the 23:00 job to run through the role-gated wrapper
#   (app.failover.run_daily_push) instead of app.daily_analysis directly, that
#   is an OPTIONAL migration — see the commented reference line at the bottom.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- NEW: 06:00 daily bi-directional sync (local instance) ---
# Runs app.sync_engine.run_sync once per day, well away from the 23:00 push.
# Env is sourced from /opt/angelina/.env by the wrapper's python process via the
# app's own os.getenv calls; we set PYTHONPATH and cd into the app dir so the
# `app.` package imports resolve exactly as under systemd.
0 6 * * * cd /opt/angelina && /opt/angelina/venv/bin/python -c "import asyncio; from app.sync_engine import run_sync; asyncio.run(run_sync())" >> /var/log/angelina/sync.log 2>&1

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL reference (commented — do NOT enable without explicit review):
# Replace the existing 23:00 daily_analysis job with the role-gated failover
# wrapper (which also stamps the heartbeat). Only enable this if you first
# REMOVE the current 23:00 daily_analysis line to avoid a double push.
# 0 23 * * * cd /opt/angelina && /opt/angelina/venv/bin/python -c "import asyncio; from app.failover import run_daily_push; asyncio.run(run_daily_push())" >> /var/log/angelina/daily.log 2>&1
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
